WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:03.246
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:03.379 --> 00:06.874
Today, we read a paper the way a curator does.

00:07.233 --> 00:09.940
What does an entity need from a paper?

00:10.073 --> 00:14.696
We read one paper on <i>DDX3X</i> and collect individuals,

00:14.829 --> 00:18.834
variants, functional data, and phenotypes.

00:19.200 --> 00:22.773
Our example is the 2015 paper by Snijders Blok

00:22.906 --> 00:28.602
and colleagues in the American
Journal of Human Genetics.

00:28.735 --> 00:33.420
You can read the full text for free in PubMed Central.

00:33.767 --> 00:39.175
The abstract reports 38 females
with 35 different <i>de novo</i> variants.

00:39.308 --> 00:40.767
A good start.

00:40.900 --> 00:47.005
For the details behind these counts,
read the methods, the patient tables

00:47.138 --> 00:49.327
and the supplement.

00:49.700 --> 00:54.899
Table 1 marks who was reported before:
four females from one study,

00:55.032 --> 00:59.259
one female from another, and one family from a third.

00:59.392 --> 01:06.099
Count each individual and family once,
however many papers report them.

01:06.467 --> 01:11.230
For <i>de novo</i> status,
check that both parents were tested.

01:11.364 --> 01:17.184
Then note the variant types:
19 predicted loss-of-function variants,

01:17.317 --> 01:20.976
15 missense and one in-frame deletion.

01:21.109 --> 01:25.034
One missense variant recurs in three females,

01:25.168 --> 01:30.144
and recurrence of a variant
is a strong genetic criterion.

01:30.500 --> 01:31.785
In three families,

01:31.918 --> 01:37.213
missense variants segregate
with intellectual disability in males;

01:37.346 --> 01:40.013
carrier females are unaffected.

01:40.146 --> 01:45.231
So one paper feeds two entities,
one per mode of inheritance:

01:45.364 --> 01:50.751
X-linked dominant for the females,
X-linked recessive for the families.

01:50.884 --> 01:53.138
Keep their counts apart.

01:53.500 --> 01:54.500
In zebrafish,

01:54.633 --> 02:01.217
all tested <i>de novo</i> variants showed
a loss-of-function effect on Wnt signaling.

02:01.351 --> 02:06.630
In this assay,
the variants from the males behaved like the wild type.

02:06.764 --> 02:10.030
Functional tests are a moderate criterion.

02:10.163 --> 02:14.300
Record what was shown, and for which variants.

02:14.667 --> 02:19.107
Table 2 lists the features of the 38 females.

02:19.240 --> 02:25.324
Enter a phenotype as a Human Phenotype Ontology term,
or HPO term,

02:25.457 --> 02:31.899
only if it occurs
in 20 percent or more of affected individuals.

02:32.032 --> 02:35.221
Hypotonia, 29 of 38, is above the line.

02:35.354 --> 02:38.993
Epilepsy, 6 of 38, is below it.

02:39.126 --> 02:45.386
Also keep the denominator:
brain MRI was reported for 37.

02:45.733 --> 02:51.017
In SysNDD, open the X-linked dominant entity.

02:51.150 --> 02:56.771
Its Clinical Synopsis keeps the frequencies,
including those below 20 percent,

02:56.904 --> 03:00.132
such as 16 percent epilepsy.

03:00.500 --> 03:06.641
Remember: count each individual and
family once, from the patient tables.

03:06.774 --> 03:11.944
Split by mode of inheritance:
one paper can feed two entities.

03:12.077 --> 03:15.705
And enter phenotypes at 20 percent or more.

03:15.838 --> 03:19.459
Keep lower frequencies in the synopsis.

03:19.800 --> 03:24.783
The SysNDD documentation lists everything to extract,

03:24.916 --> 03:28.520
in the chapter Research a gene and read a paper.
